WEBVTT

00:14.535 --> 00:15.953
Yumeka…

00:17.788 --> 00:20.708
No way. I can't believe it.

00:20.791 --> 00:23.711
Natsu finally got herself a boyfriend.

00:28.049 --> 00:30.968
That means you've given up
on winning nationals.

00:35.389 --> 00:36.849
I haven't given up.

00:40.019 --> 00:41.103
I see.

00:41.729 --> 00:44.106
You always did manage to do it all.

00:44.690 --> 00:47.526
You couldn't even dribble the ball
when you first started,

00:47.610 --> 00:49.361
but now you're the star player.

00:50.946 --> 00:51.947
On top of that,

00:52.031 --> 00:54.533
you even have a fulfilling private life.

00:54.617 --> 00:56.243
You really are something, aren't you?

00:57.745 --> 00:59.246
Hey.

00:59.330 --> 01:00.956
There was a nicer way to say that.

01:01.040 --> 01:02.416
What? I said it normal!

01:02.500 --> 01:05.503
This is why your English grade
was so abysmal this term.

01:05.586 --> 01:07.296
For your information, I got an A.

01:07.963 --> 01:09.215
Sorry about that.

01:09.298 --> 01:12.134
She must be excited from the altitude.
We'll be off.

01:12.218 --> 01:13.761
What am I, a monkey?

01:13.844 --> 01:15.012
A monkey's intelligence--

01:15.096 --> 01:16.639
Spare me the trivia.

01:16.722 --> 01:17.807
Fine.

01:21.352 --> 01:22.812
<i>She glared at me.</i>

01:24.897 --> 01:25.773
I'm sorry.

01:25.856 --> 01:27.316
Uh, who was that?

01:28.150 --> 01:30.236
A former teammate of mine.

01:30.319 --> 01:32.988
She was at Eimei
through the end of middle school.

01:33.072 --> 01:35.241
But then, she transferred out
for high school.

01:37.201 --> 01:38.536
I've seen her before.

01:39.912 --> 01:41.831
And I've seen her play.

01:41.914 --> 01:44.708
<i>People even said</i>
<i>she was better than Chinatsu.</i>

01:46.877 --> 01:49.338
I had heard the rumors that she quit, but…

01:49.922 --> 01:51.590
I didn't know she was like that.

01:56.387 --> 01:57.513
It's getting late.

01:57.596 --> 01:59.473
We should probably get going.

01:59.557 --> 02:00.641
Good idea.

02:11.569 --> 02:12.695
About earlier…

02:13.904 --> 02:15.990
You can do it, Chinatsu.

02:16.073 --> 02:17.992
You can win nationals.

02:20.578 --> 02:22.121
Mmm.

02:23.038 --> 02:24.456
Of course.

02:28.460 --> 02:30.588
How many more stations?

02:30.671 --> 02:31.964
Just three, I think.

02:34.091 --> 02:36.677
<i>Our shoulders are touching.</i>
<i>Our shoulders are touching.</i>

02:42.600 --> 02:43.767
Oh!

02:44.435 --> 02:45.728
You can sit here!

02:45.811 --> 02:47.563
Oh, thank you so much.

02:52.109 --> 02:53.360
Mmm.

03:03.537 --> 03:07.666
BLUE BOX SEASON 2

04:30.040 --> 04:31.625
EIMEI PRIVATE HIGH SCHOOL

04:31.709 --> 04:32.960
EPISODE 27
ADMIRATION

04:33.043 --> 04:35.713
Come on, hustle!

04:35.796 --> 04:37.965
Yuki, mark Nagisa!

04:38.048 --> 04:40.718
We won't qualify
for the Winter Cup playing like that.

04:41.427 --> 04:43.595
- Kano, look around you!
- Right!

04:44.305 --> 04:48.142
I heard that the Basketball's Winter Cup
is happening on Christmas Day this year.

04:48.225 --> 04:49.685
I know that, Kyo.

04:49.768 --> 04:53.397
They'll have to eat their holiday meals
with the team. That's kind of sad.

04:53.480 --> 04:55.232
Wow. Way to be blunt about it.

04:55.316 --> 04:58.569
Last year, we hung out
and celebrated with our classmates,

04:58.652 --> 05:00.988
- but this year…
- Uh…

05:01.613 --> 05:03.824
This year, we'll partake in practice.

05:03.907 --> 05:05.576
- What?
- There's no good reason

05:05.659 --> 05:07.995
why we can't have a practice
on Christmas Eve.

05:08.078 --> 05:10.164
And I'm not saying that
'cause I'm utterly lonely

05:10.247 --> 05:12.458
or 'cause I hate people
who have girlfriends.

05:12.541 --> 05:15.919
Just think of my holiday practice schedule
as an early Christmas present.

05:18.630 --> 05:20.716
I know you're pumped up, Haryu.

05:20.799 --> 05:22.426
Huh? Yeah, sure.

05:22.509 --> 05:25.387
I bet sissy is gonna have
some complaints about it.

05:27.514 --> 05:29.516
Anyway, I'm gonna hit the weight room.

05:29.600 --> 05:31.685
All right, I'll come with you.

05:36.273 --> 05:38.275
<i>Christmas practice…</i>

05:38.359 --> 05:41.195
<i>So, he won't be spending Christmas</i>
<i>with Chinatsu.</i>

05:42.363 --> 05:44.740
<i>Knock it off!</i>
<i>I shouldn't be eavesdropping.</i>

05:44.823 --> 05:46.575
<i>But still, I heard what I heard.</i>

05:46.658 --> 05:49.203
<i>Why is it that hope that never dies?</i>

05:49.787 --> 05:53.957
Hey, Hina. Our practice on Christmas Eve
is voluntary, so are you going?

05:55.751 --> 05:56.585
I'll be there.

05:57.294 --> 05:59.213
TRAINING ROOM

06:03.300 --> 06:04.426
Um, hey, Haryu?

06:04.510 --> 06:05.677
Huh?

06:05.761 --> 06:07.721
I have something I wanna ask you.

06:08.472 --> 06:09.765
What is it?

06:09.848 --> 06:11.975
- This better not be stupid.
- No! It's not!

06:12.601 --> 06:14.436
Do you remember Yumeka from basketball?

06:16.563 --> 06:19.650
<i>Wow, Haryu</i>
<i>has such a disgusted look on his face.</i>

06:19.733 --> 06:23.737
Haven't heard someone mention
the Queen of Sarcasm's name in a while.

06:23.821 --> 06:25.197
It's just that…

06:25.280 --> 06:28.117
- Well, I met Yumeka the other day.
- Huh?

06:28.200 --> 06:29.368
With Chi?

06:29.451 --> 06:31.161
Uh-huh, that's right.

06:31.245 --> 06:32.788
Wait, how'd you know?

06:32.871 --> 06:33.872
Doesn't matter.

06:34.665 --> 06:36.792
I'm guessing it was kinda awkward?

06:36.875 --> 06:38.085
Uh, yeah.

06:38.168 --> 06:40.921
I was wondering
if you knew the reason she quit.

06:41.004 --> 06:43.382
I don't know the exact details either.

06:44.216 --> 06:48.137
<i>She does have a lot of pride,</i>
<i>and is not the type to ask for advice.</i>

06:49.304 --> 06:51.682
So I don't think
it's as simple as hating basketball.

06:52.933 --> 06:54.184
You know…

06:54.268 --> 06:57.271
the person who took it the hardest
was definitely Chi.

06:58.355 --> 07:00.190
<i>They've known each other</i>
<i>since they were seven</i>

07:00.274 --> 07:01.775
<i>and were on the same junior team.</i>

07:02.359 --> 07:05.696
Chinatsu is always
at morning practice early, right?

07:05.779 --> 07:06.780
Uh-huh.

07:07.531 --> 07:08.949
<i>She told me…</i>

07:09.032 --> 07:12.286
<i>She started doing that specifically</i>
<i>to catch up to Yumeka.</i>

07:15.456 --> 07:19.251
<i>That means Chinatsu</i>
<i>is who she is because of Yumeka!</i>

07:20.752 --> 07:22.379
<i>I wonder…</i>

07:23.547 --> 07:26.550
<i>how she must have felt</i>
<i>to hear her friend and role model…</i>

07:27.134 --> 07:29.720
<i>accuse her of giving up on basketball?</i>

07:30.387 --> 07:33.182
<i>I can only imagine</i>
<i>what was going through her head.</i>

07:35.017 --> 07:37.436
INOMATA

07:38.479 --> 07:40.439
Ow, it hurts!

07:40.522 --> 07:42.441
What is it? A cavity?

07:43.192 --> 07:46.528
It's because you've been spacing out
while brushing your teeth lately.

07:47.321 --> 07:48.989
I'm going to the dentist.

07:49.072 --> 07:51.450
- Oh, that place closed down.
- What?

07:51.533 --> 07:54.286
There's a clinic near Azumabara Station.

07:54.369 --> 07:56.246
Why don't you give that spot a go?

07:57.039 --> 07:58.207
Okay…

08:03.045 --> 08:04.963
KIKUCHI DENTAL CLINIC

08:05.756 --> 08:06.798
Excuse me.

08:08.091 --> 08:10.093
I made an appointment over the phone.

08:10.177 --> 08:12.095
Do you have your insurance card?

08:12.179 --> 08:13.305
Oh, yes.

08:14.431 --> 08:15.474
Thank you.

08:17.559 --> 08:18.519
Inomata…

08:19.811 --> 08:21.730
Uh…

08:22.481 --> 08:23.732
Oh!

08:25.234 --> 08:27.236
Taiki Inomata.

08:33.158 --> 08:34.743
<i>This is awkward.</i>

08:35.327 --> 08:36.745
<i>I'll turn on the TV.</i>

08:36.828 --> 08:40.499
- <i>In a few moments…</i>
- Don't touch that without asking.

08:40.582 --> 08:41.583
PLEASE FEEL FREE TO WATCH

08:41.667 --> 08:42.501
<i>Huh?</i>

08:44.711 --> 08:46.547
<i>She hates me.</i>

08:46.630 --> 08:49.716
<i>Is it 'cause she thinks</i>
<i>I'm Chinatsu's boyfriend?</i>

08:49.800 --> 08:51.426
<i>I have to clear that up.</i>

08:51.510 --> 08:53.387
<i>Although I'm not obligated to tell her.</i>

08:54.096 --> 08:56.265
<i>Besides, I should be her boyfriend!</i>

08:56.348 --> 08:58.850
<i>Why didn't I ask her out</i>
<i>when I had the chance?</i>

08:58.934 --> 09:00.394
Mr. Inomata?

09:00.477 --> 09:01.937
- You're next.
- Oh, yes!

09:05.732 --> 09:06.900
Mmm…

09:06.984 --> 09:09.236
You're wearing mismatching slippers.

09:09.319 --> 09:10.279
Huh?

09:10.362 --> 09:12.322
Oh. I'll go change them.

09:12.406 --> 09:14.491
- You can just keep that pair on.
- Ah!

09:14.575 --> 09:16.493
And quit fooling around.

09:20.038 --> 09:22.749
Oh my, looks like your cavity
reached the nerve!

09:23.834 --> 09:27.421
<i>That does it.</i>
<i>I'm gonna give this place a bad review!</i>

09:28.338 --> 09:29.840
You take care now!

09:30.340 --> 09:31.925
Thank you very much.

09:36.346 --> 09:38.265
That'll be 1,900 yen.

09:39.224 --> 09:41.310
<i>The dentist told me I'll have to come back</i>

09:41.393 --> 09:42.728
<i>for a few more appointments.</i>

09:43.228 --> 09:44.354
KIKUCHI DENTAL CLINIC

09:44.438 --> 09:46.815
<i>So more chances</i>
<i>of running into her, I guess.</i>

09:54.239 --> 09:55.157
BARLEY TEA

09:56.992 --> 09:59.494
You're drinking juice
right after a filling?

10:01.997 --> 10:03.415
Oh, it's barley tea.

10:03.999 --> 10:06.668
Even if it's tea,
it probably still has sugar in it.

10:07.502 --> 10:08.420
Huh?

10:08.503 --> 10:09.880
Oh, you're right!

10:11.256 --> 10:13.091
That's why you're the dentist.

10:14.092 --> 10:17.304
Not a dentist. I'm just working part-time
as a receptionist.

10:17.387 --> 10:18.597
Part-time?

10:19.556 --> 10:21.850
I wanted to earn
some extra spending money.

10:22.893 --> 10:25.312
Is that why you quit basketball?

10:28.148 --> 10:28.982
Uh…

10:30.359 --> 10:31.943
Sorry. Never mind.

10:32.027 --> 10:33.487
I'll just head home.

10:33.570 --> 10:34.780
That's not why.

10:36.406 --> 10:39.076
I quit basketball
'cause I started to hate Chinatsu.

10:41.912 --> 10:42.746
Huh?

10:42.829 --> 10:44.748
I was also getting tired of playing.

10:44.831 --> 10:46.583
I just felt like I'd had enough.

10:47.167 --> 10:48.335
That can't be.

10:48.418 --> 10:49.503
Why not?

10:49.586 --> 10:52.714
You think it's impossible for someone
to hate your girlfriend?

10:52.798 --> 10:54.675
No, that's not it!

10:55.258 --> 10:56.677
<i>Back in middle school,</i>

10:56.760 --> 10:58.428
<i>they were so close.</i>

11:00.055 --> 11:01.431
<i>But now…</i>

11:02.974 --> 11:06.186
You didn't tell Chinatsu
you hated her, right?

11:07.854 --> 11:08.939
I did.

11:20.659 --> 11:22.452
Hey, Taiki. Welcome back.

11:27.082 --> 11:28.792
It's freezing out here.

11:32.295 --> 11:33.964
Where are you headed, Chinatsu?

11:34.047 --> 11:34.923
Just walking.

11:35.006 --> 11:36.174
In this cold?

11:36.258 --> 11:39.094
Exactly. I want to experience
the winter weather.

11:39.886 --> 11:41.012
Wanna come with me?

11:44.975 --> 11:46.309
Where are we going?

11:46.393 --> 11:47.477
Nowhere.

11:49.396 --> 11:50.772
<i>My gut's telling me…</i>

11:51.314 --> 11:53.817
<i>I probably shouldn't mention</i>
<i>seeing Yumeka.</i>

11:54.484 --> 11:55.360
Oh.

11:56.403 --> 11:57.612
I smell curry.

11:58.196 --> 12:00.115
Really? You smell it right now?

12:00.198 --> 12:02.701
Yeah, it smells like
the veggies are being stewed

12:02.784 --> 12:05.203
- before adding the roux.
- Oddly specific.

12:05.287 --> 12:07.622
Oh, and now I can smell shampoo.

12:09.624 --> 12:11.126
I'm home.

12:11.710 --> 12:14.379
- You know, it's kind of strange.
- Huh?

12:14.463 --> 12:17.924
When I was looking out
from the observation deck the other day,

12:18.008 --> 12:20.385
every light in the city seemed so small.

12:21.303 --> 12:24.890
But now, seeing it all up close,
everything's so big and dense.

12:25.474 --> 12:26.975
Somehow, it's reassuring.

12:28.727 --> 12:29.644
Oh, by the way…

12:30.687 --> 12:32.481
Sorry about the other day.

12:32.564 --> 12:36.401
I guess my… acquaintance
made you feel kind of bad, huh?

12:36.485 --> 12:38.904
No! No, not at all.

12:39.654 --> 12:41.406
I'm glad to hear that.

12:43.992 --> 12:45.368
You and her were friends

12:45.452 --> 12:48.455
and played on the same basketball team
when you were little, right?

12:50.207 --> 12:52.167
Yeah, since second grade.

12:53.376 --> 12:56.171
Even back then, she was like a hurricane.

12:57.672 --> 13:00.008
<i>I'd barely played catch by that point,</i>

13:00.091 --> 13:02.969
<i>so I was fascinated</i>
<i>watching professional basketball.</i>

13:04.846 --> 13:05.889
Hey, Mom,

13:05.972 --> 13:07.432
I wanna do that!

13:08.725 --> 13:11.269
Make sure to speak up
when you're introducing yourself.

13:11.353 --> 13:12.187
Mmm!

13:14.105 --> 13:14.940
Hi…

13:15.023 --> 13:16.983
<i>She was the same age as me.</i>

13:17.067 --> 13:17.901
Go, Yumeka!

13:17.984 --> 13:20.403
<i>She had total control of the ball,</i>

13:20.487 --> 13:23.448
<i>ran right down the court,</i>
<i>and hit a lay-up like it was nothing.</i>

13:25.784 --> 13:27.160
<i>I deeply admired her,</i>

13:27.869 --> 13:28.995
<i>from the moment I saw her.</i>

13:33.959 --> 13:37.170
Oh. Hey! Are you a new girl?

13:38.547 --> 13:39.923
Oh…

13:41.299 --> 13:42.425
You know what?

13:43.093 --> 13:45.679
You sort of look like a board game piece.

13:46.346 --> 13:47.472
Board game piece?

13:49.683 --> 13:52.811
Come on, Yumeka!
Is that how we say hello to someone?

13:52.894 --> 13:54.938
It's true though!
I played as her yesterday!

13:57.983 --> 13:58.817
She did?

14:00.735 --> 14:02.445
Keep it up, Chinatsu!

14:02.529 --> 14:03.697
Right!

14:03.780 --> 14:05.490
Try to loosen your wrist.

14:06.032 --> 14:07.701
Ah.

14:14.124 --> 14:15.959
Yumeka is good, isn't she?

14:16.835 --> 14:18.461
That girl has talent.

14:19.379 --> 14:21.840
She has a wide field of vision
for her age,

14:21.923 --> 14:24.217
and her ball handling is amazing.

14:25.552 --> 14:28.263
But if you work hard,
I think you'll catch up to her.

14:29.848 --> 14:31.057
Break time!

14:32.601 --> 14:35.145
Next, we'll practice passing the ball.

14:35.896 --> 14:37.397
Did you hear that?

14:37.480 --> 14:38.899
She said I'll learn to pass!

14:38.982 --> 14:40.191
That's great, honey.

14:42.068 --> 14:42.944
Uh.

14:43.028 --> 14:43.987
Oh.

14:48.074 --> 14:50.243
<i>The coach said she had talent,</i>

14:51.620 --> 14:56.583
<i>but Yumeka probably spends more time</i>
<i>with the ball than anyone else here.</i>

15:09.512 --> 15:12.682
Uh.

15:16.269 --> 15:19.439
The new girl
still isn't getting any better.

15:19.522 --> 15:21.316
The girl from Kita Elementary?

15:21.399 --> 15:22.525
Yeah, exactly.

15:22.609 --> 15:24.277
She's totally hopeless.

15:24.361 --> 15:26.196
She can't even hit the backboard.

15:26.279 --> 15:28.782
I mean, I could do that on the first day.

15:28.865 --> 15:30.700
Her passes aren't good either.

15:30.784 --> 15:32.702
I hope I don't get paired with her.

15:33.286 --> 15:35.163
That might be a little too mean.

15:36.539 --> 15:37.958
I'm going on ahead!

15:38.041 --> 15:39.250
Huh? Mmm.

15:40.627 --> 15:44.381
Yumeka doesn't really like to stick around
when we talk about that stuff.

15:45.757 --> 15:48.301
I guess we all probably
look the same to her.

15:48.385 --> 15:49.970
You, and I, and the new girl.

15:50.887 --> 15:52.973
<i>That's how good Yumeka is.</i>

16:04.776 --> 16:06.236
Oh. Hi, Yumeka.

16:06.319 --> 16:07.988
Uh-- Hey there.

16:11.700 --> 16:13.243
Whoa!

16:18.581 --> 16:20.083
You suck at this.

16:23.336 --> 16:24.504
Like that.

16:27.048 --> 16:29.009
Wait, how did you do that?

16:29.718 --> 16:31.928
You know, like this. Whoosh.

16:32.512 --> 16:33.722
Show me again!

16:34.597 --> 16:37.642
Do I have to teach you everything?

16:37.726 --> 16:39.269
Like this?

16:40.228 --> 16:41.688
I just showed you!

16:43.606 --> 16:44.774
And then…

16:44.858 --> 16:47.110
Yumeka made this amazing shot!

16:47.193 --> 16:48.778
She's so cool!

16:51.448 --> 16:53.283
Chinatsu, I'm counting on you.

16:53.867 --> 16:54.993
A uniform!

16:55.076 --> 16:56.494
My own uniform!

16:56.578 --> 16:57.871
Yumeka, I made the team!

16:57.954 --> 16:59.289
Uh, yeah. I see that.

17:08.548 --> 17:09.966
That's so annoying!

17:10.050 --> 17:10.925
- Ah…
- In what world

17:11.009 --> 17:13.094
do I lose my starting spot to that girl?

17:13.178 --> 17:16.264
I started playing basketball
way before she did!

17:17.223 --> 17:19.768
She only got that uniform out of pity!

17:19.851 --> 17:21.436
Yuna, please, calm down.

17:23.354 --> 17:25.523
Instead of complaining,
why don't you practice?

17:25.607 --> 17:27.233
Huh? Yumeka…

17:27.317 --> 17:29.778
At least, that's why Chinatsu's a starter.

17:29.861 --> 17:31.613
She put in all the hard work,

17:32.197 --> 17:34.407
and that's why she has the uniform now.

17:34.491 --> 17:36.034
I have talent,

17:36.117 --> 17:38.870
so I don't know what it's like
to admire someone else's.

17:39.496 --> 17:41.706
But her ability to work hard…

17:42.707 --> 17:44.167
I do admire that.

17:49.172 --> 17:50.840
<i>She was like a hurricane.</i>

17:51.758 --> 17:54.177
<i>She didn't let anything get in her way.</i>

17:54.260 --> 17:57.138
<i>And she drew people in with her charisma.</i>

17:57.972 --> 17:59.891
A recommendation to Eimei?

18:00.600 --> 18:01.768
You should come too.

18:02.352 --> 18:03.520
Mmm.

18:03.603 --> 18:07.524
<i>She made you feel like everything</i>
<i>would be okay if you just followed her.</i>

18:08.191 --> 18:09.484
I admired her.

18:10.693 --> 18:12.987
I wanted to be like Yumeka,

18:13.071 --> 18:14.781
so I practiced nonstop.

18:18.243 --> 18:20.245
Even now, I sometimes think…

18:21.663 --> 18:23.832
<i>"If only Yumeka was on my team."</i>

18:26.251 --> 18:29.796
<i>It doesn't matter</i>
<i>if it's an individual or team sport.</i>

18:30.463 --> 18:32.382
<i>Every athlete's the same,</i>

18:32.465 --> 18:35.176
<i>'cause we're competing against ourselves.</i>

18:37.345 --> 18:39.556
- So are you really quitting?
- Yeah.

18:39.639 --> 18:41.266
What'd your parents say?

18:41.349 --> 18:43.059
They have nothing to do with it.

18:43.643 --> 18:46.771
What about Chinatsu from class B?

18:46.855 --> 18:49.065
You've played with her for a while, right?

18:49.149 --> 18:50.817
I don't care about her.

18:50.900 --> 18:53.570
Ever since we were little,
it was always "Yumeka, Yumeka…"

18:54.154 --> 18:55.572
Ah…

18:56.865 --> 18:58.324
And I hate her.

19:03.079 --> 19:04.831
Yes! Rebound!

19:04.914 --> 19:06.332
Nice play!

19:06.416 --> 19:08.042
Okay, ten-minute break.

19:10.920 --> 19:12.589
<i>I have to get better.</i>

19:12.672 --> 19:14.090
<i>A lot better.</i>

19:16.176 --> 19:17.844
- Too slow!
- Ah.

19:18.928 --> 19:20.096
Where are you hitting? Right!

19:20.180 --> 19:21.848
Left side!

19:21.931 --> 19:23.308
Nice job!

19:27.437 --> 19:28.354
Ah.

19:29.981 --> 19:31.608
Hmm? Uh.

19:36.279 --> 19:37.238
Mmm.

19:37.322 --> 19:38.489
Ah, ah.

19:38.573 --> 19:39.741
Ah…

19:40.408 --> 19:42.744
Wait, I obviously can't eat this!

19:50.585 --> 19:53.838
I got first place
in the gym class race today!

19:56.507 --> 19:58.092
<i>There's no way.</i>

19:58.176 --> 20:02.680
<i>I can't imagine Yumeka</i>
<i>being able to</i>… <i>hate Chinatsu.</i>

20:03.848 --> 20:07.393
<i>Maybe she got injured</i>
<i>so she couldn't play basketball anymore.</i>

20:08.228 --> 20:11.689
<i>And acting that way towards Chinatsu</i>
<i>was her way of hiding it.</i>

20:15.944 --> 20:17.362
- Darn!
- Too easy.

20:17.445 --> 20:20.114
She's able to play basketball just fine!

20:20.198 --> 20:21.115
Mmm.

20:22.158 --> 20:23.451
That's it for today.

20:23.534 --> 20:24.369
Come on!

20:24.953 --> 20:26.788
You owe me a rematch then!

20:28.456 --> 20:30.083
You play sometimes?

20:30.166 --> 20:31.542
Just for fun.

20:34.295 --> 20:37.382
Well, but isn't it a waste,
you playing just for fun?

20:37.966 --> 20:39.259
Everyone says…

20:39.342 --> 20:41.386
you're a genius player, Yumeka.

20:42.470 --> 20:45.098
I guess that's how it looks
to other people.

20:45.682 --> 20:48.601
Although I did seem to pick things up
faster than most.

20:48.685 --> 20:49.769
<i>Was that snark?</i>

20:49.852 --> 20:51.938
And I did have really great ball control.

20:52.021 --> 20:53.398
<i>Definitely snark!</i>

20:53.481 --> 20:54.899
However…

20:56.150 --> 20:59.862
<i>there are tons of people out there</i>
<i>who are better than me at basketball.</i>

21:01.698 --> 21:03.908
That may be true, but still…

21:04.575 --> 21:06.244
Have you ever thought about it?

21:06.327 --> 21:09.664
What your life will look like
if you keep only focusing on sports?

21:10.290 --> 21:12.166
<i>What do you have to gain</i>
<i>by pushing yourself</i>

21:12.250 --> 21:14.669
<i>at practice every single day?</i>

21:15.503 --> 21:17.130
<i>It's not like we can go pro.</i>

21:17.213 --> 21:19.924
<i>Only the best players</i>
<i>leave the tournament smiling.</i>

21:20.591 --> 21:22.302
<i>Why would you go out of your way…</i>

21:23.052 --> 21:24.345
<i>to work so hard?</i>

21:25.680 --> 21:27.682
What kind of an excuse is that?

21:27.765 --> 21:28.725
Huh?

21:28.808 --> 21:32.312
I mean, you knew about all that
from the start, didn't you?

21:32.395 --> 21:34.772
And still, you wanted to play and win.

21:35.732 --> 21:38.818
To chase down the ball in front of you
because it's fun.

21:38.901 --> 21:40.820
So why quit?

21:40.903 --> 21:42.989
I think the answer is simple.

21:43.656 --> 21:46.659
It's not about other people
or how you performed.

21:47.618 --> 21:49.787
You quit because you were talented!

21:50.288 --> 21:52.415
<i>You were so used to being good,</i>

21:52.498 --> 21:54.417
<i>you couldn't stand failure.</i>

21:54.500 --> 21:57.337
<i>If you ask me, that's a waste.</i>

21:57.420 --> 22:00.340
You would've had more chances
when you got to high school.

22:00.423 --> 22:03.092
It's only natural
that there are people better than you.

22:03.718 --> 22:05.345
But that's not the point.

22:05.428 --> 22:07.221
That's not the point at all.

22:11.726 --> 22:12.727
- Well…
- Ah.

22:13.394 --> 22:17.231
It's easy to say the right thing
when you're watching from the sidelines.
